# Setup Guide - {{ project_name }}

## System Requirements

- **OS**: macOS, Linux, or Windows
- **JDK**: Version {{ jdk_version }} or higher
- **Android Studio**: Latest stable version
- **Gradle**: {{ gradle_version }}

## Installation Steps

### 1. Environment Setup

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/{{ github_actor }}/{{ target_repo }}.git
cd {{ target_repo }}

# Set JAVA_HOME (if not already set)
export JAVA_HOME=/path/to/jdk{{ jdk_version }}
export PATH=$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH
```

### 2. Android SDK Setup

1. Open Android Studio
2. Go to SDK Manager
3. Install API level {{ target_sdk }}
4. Accept all licenses

### 3. Build Project

```bash
# Build debug APK
./gradlew assembleDebug

# Build release APK
./gradlew assembleRelease
```

### 4. Run on Device/Emulator

```bash
# List connected devices
adb devices

# Install debug APK
./gradlew installDebug
```

## Troubleshooting

### Gradle Build Issues
```bash
./gradlew clean assembleDebug
```

### Run Tests
```bash
# Unit tests
./gradlew test

# Instrumented tests
./gradlew connectedAndroidTest
```

## IDE Configuration

### Android Studio
1. File → Open → select the project directory
2. Let Gradle sync complete
3. Set SDK to API {{ target_sdk }} in File → Project Structure
4. Run the app on a device or emulator

